faq:
  - q: "What is the LinkedIn About section?"
    a: "The About section is the narrative summary of your LinkedIn profile — equivalent to a resume's professional summary but longer and more personal. It appears below your headline and photo and is where you establish your professional identity, strongest outcomes, domain specialization, and what you are looking for. It is the highest-value real estate on your profile after your headline."
  - q: "What should the first line of your LinkedIn About section say?"
    a: "The first line is critical — it is what appears in search results and preview cards before the reader clicks 'see more.' It should immediately establish your professional identity. Strong: 'Staff Software Engineer specializing in platform infrastructure and distributed systems.' Weak: 'I am a passionate professional who loves solving problems.' The first line must make your level and specialization clear before anyone clicks further."
  - q: "How long should the LinkedIn About section be?"
    a: "150–300 words. Long enough to establish credibility and give recruiters a clear picture of who you are. Short enough to be fully read. Below 100 words signals a low-effort profile. Above 400 words with no line breaks loses readers. LinkedIn shows only the first ~220 characters before truncating — your opening must hook before 'see more.'"
  - q: "Should you write your LinkedIn About section in first or third person?"
    a: "First person. Third person on LinkedIn reads as formal and strange — it is a personal profile, not a press release. Write as if you are speaking directly to the reader. 'I build distributed systems at scale' reads more credibly than 'John builds distributed systems at scale.'"
  - q: "How do you end a LinkedIn About section?"
    a: "With a targeting statement and call to action. Example: 'Currently exploring Staff+ engineering and engineering leadership roles at growth-stage B2B companies. Happy to connect if you're building in infrastructure or platform engineering.' This tells recruiters exactly what to do with your profile."
  - q: "What is the LinkedIn About section formula?"
    a: "Four parts: (1) Who you are professionally — level, function, domain. This is your opening hook. (2) What you have accomplished — 2–3 specific outcomes with numbers. (3) What you specialize in — the intersection of your strongest skills and most valuable problems you solve. (4) What you are targeting — a specific targeting statement that gives recruiters direction."
